@prefix ag: <http://example.org/agora#> .

#  The supplier's PRIVATE beliefs — its terms as a genuine seller, not a stake-free utility.
#
#  It composed ag:Hosting and ag:Actuation, so only those modules' terms appear. There is no
#  target here and no cadence: it neither wants anything watered nor perceives anything.

##  ag:Hosting — how it runs a round
ag:supplier
    ag:offerQuantityL 2.0 ;      # what it puts up
    ag:reservePricePerL 0.20 ;   # its floor; buyers never see the reasoning
    ag:bidWindowS 3 ;            # how long it waits for bids before matching
    ag:roundCooldownS 30 .       # it will not open rounds faster than this

##  How often it says how it is — belief base size, reading freshness, silent write failures.
#   Omit this line and the agent reports nothing; see agora/metrics.py.
ag:supplier ag:metricsIntervalS 60 .

##  Self-review — how often at the very least, and how much room it gives itself.
#   Omit ag:reviewIntervalS and it never revises anything: its beliefs stay exactly what
#   genesis wrote. The commitment is the SELF constraint — narrower than the constitution's
#   10..900 — so the figure above is a first pick rather than a floor, and this says how far
#   the agent will let itself wander from it. See decisions/a-belief-is-a-pick-within-a-range.
ag:supplier ag:reviewIntervalS 300 .
#   No ag:slowSleepS to commit about: this agent states no cadence.
